CON-09: keep pollutant in ponded surface water when the water evaporates

findPondedLoads() mixed the ponded mass with rain and run-on over the
step's water volume, removed the infiltrated and runoff mass, and then
rebuilt the ponded mass as cPonded * depth * area. The pollutant in the
water that evaporated during the step (cPonded * Vevap) was dropped with
no ledger entry: 0.1 in of rain at 10 mg/L that evaporates from
depression storage gave a 100 % runoff quality continuity error. Keep the
mass that infiltration and runoff did not remove, so evaporation
concentrates the ponded water (reference manual eq. 4-11, note 4).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-09_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/surfqual.c b/src/legacy/engine/surfqual.c
index 893b975..e7d0edf 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/surfqual.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/surfqual.c
@@ -461,8 +461,9 @@ void findPondedLoads(int j, double tStep)
                                         bmpRemoval * Pollut[p].mcf);
             wOutflow -= bmpRemoval;
 
-            // --- update ponded mass (using newly computed ponded depth)
-            Subcatch[j].pondedQual[p] = cPonded * subcatch_getDepth(j) * nonLidArea;
+            // --- update ponded mass: what infiltration and runoff did not
+            //     remove stays (evaporation takes water, not pollutant)
+            Subcatch[j].pondedQual[p] = wPonded;
             OutflowLoad[p] += wOutflow;
         }
     }
